# fixedbugs, defect 563, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 204's R1; the
# compiler-engineer's `dual`).
#
# Two headers each define `K` only where no header before them has: 5 in
# `fixedbugs-563-p.h`, 9 in `fixedbugs-563-q.h`. No macro is defined twice,
# so clang says nothing in either order, and the order the groups are
# written in is the one that decides: `p` first, so `K` is 5 in both. The
# case beside this one writes them the other way and prints 9 and 109.
extern "fixedbugs-563-p.h"
    function pk() -> i32

extern "fixedbugs-563-q.h"
    function qk() -> i32

function main()
    print(pk())
    print(qk())
